1
00:05:29,032 --> 00:05:35,032
The world is yours.

2
00:10:58,064 --> 00:11:04,064
Scarface is a action, crime, drama film directed by Brian De Palma.

3
00:16:27,096 --> 00:16:33,096
After getting a green card in exchange for assassinating a Cuban government
official, Tony Montana stakes a claim on the drug trade in Miami.

4
00:21:56,129 --> 00:22:02,129
Viciously murdering anyone who stands in his way, Tony eventually becomes the biggest drug
lord in the state, controlling nearly all the cocaine that comes through Miami.

5
00:27:25,161 --> 00:27:31,161
But increased pressure from the police, wars with Colombian drug cartels and his own
drug-fueled paranoia serve to fuel the flames of his eventual downfall.

6
00:32:54,193 --> 00:33:00,193
Tony Montana, played by Al Pacino.

7
00:38:23,225 --> 00:38:29,225
Manny Ray, played by Steven Bauer.

8
00:43:52,258 --> 00:43:58,258
Elvira, played by Michelle Pfeiffer.

9
00:49:21,290 --> 00:49:27,290
Gina, played by Mary Elizabeth Mastrantonio.

10
00:54:50,322 --> 00:54:56,322
Frank Lopez, played by Robert Loggia.

11
01:00:19,354 --> 01:00:25,354
Mama Montana, played by Miriam Colon.

12
01:05:48,387 --> 01:05:54,387
Scarface is a 1983 American crime drama film directed by
Brian De Palma, and written by Oliver Stone.

13
01:11:17,419 --> 01:11:23,419
It is a remake of the 1932 film of the same name.

14
01:16:46,451 --> 01:16:52,451
It stars Al Pacino as Cuban refugee Tony Montana, who arrives in Miami
during the Mariel boatlift and becomes a powerful drug lord.

15
01:22:15,483 --> 01:22:21,483
Pacino worked with producer Martin Bregman to develop the project.

16
01:27:44,516 --> 01:27:50,516
Bregman and Sidney Lumet both conceived the idea of
setting the story during the boatlift.

17
01:33:13,548 --> 01:33:19,548
Lumet was initially hired to direct the film but left, feeling that it was
too violent and wanted it to be more of a political film.

18
01:38:42,580 --> 01:38:48,580
De Palma replaced Lumet as director and Bregman hired Stone to write the script.

19
01:44:11,612 --> 01:44:17,612
Stone, who had been struggling with his own cocaine
addiction at the time, wrote the script in Paris.

20
01:49:40,645 --> 01:49:46,645
The film was initially going to be entirely shot in Miami, but the Cuban community denied
requests to film there, feeling that the script portrayed them in a bad light.

21
01:55:09,677 --> 01:55:15,677
Filming took place from November 1982 to May 1983 in
Los Angeles and two weeks in Miami.

22
02:00:38,709 --> 02:00:44,709
The film's soundtrack and score was composed by Giorgio Moroder.

23
02:06:07,741 --> 02:06:13,741
Scarface premiered in New York City on December 1, 1983, and was
released on December 9 by Universal Pictures.

24
02:11:36,774 --> 02:11:42,774
The film was a commercial success, grossing $66 million.

25
02:17:05,806 --> 02:17:11,806
Initial critical response was negative due to its extreme
violence and depiction of stereotypes.

26
02:22:34,838 --> 02:22:40,838
However, in the years that followed, some critics have reappraised it, and it
is now considered to be one of the greatest films ever made.

27
02:28:03,870 --> 02:28:09,870
Screenwriters and directors such as Martin Scorsese have praised the film, and it has been referenced extensively in
pop culture, especially in hip-hop culture, as well as comic books, television programs and video games.

28
02:33:32,903 --> 02:33:38,903
The film is regarded as a cult classic.

29
02:39:01,935 --> 02:39:07,935
The film explores themes of corruption, sibling
relationship, miami, florida, cuba, loss of loved one.

30
02:44:30,967 --> 02:44:36,967
The tone is emotional.
